# Readable code and OWASP

Clarity and security are both required. Do not hide access checks in a clever one-liner. Do not skip a control to keep a function short — extract a named helper (`requireOwnerRole`, `denyClientWrites`, `rejectInvalidFile`) and comment *why*. Full mapping: `SECURITY.md`.

## Access control (OWASP A01)

- Authorize on the **server**. Vue `v-if` and router guards are not security.
- DDP methods: `check` / `Match`, then login/role gates, then the write. Use `userIsInRoleAsync` and `Meteor.callAsync`.
- Publications: if the caller may not see rows, `return this.ready()`. Never `Collection.find()` with no filter.
- Package collections deny client `insert` / `update` / `remove`. Do not add `insecure` or a permissive `allow`.
- Do not pass a client-supplied Mongo modifier through to `updateAsync`.

## Uploads, injection, secrets (A02–A04, A07, file upload)

- MIME allowlist and size limits are **server** checks. Parent document must exist before GridFS writes.
- `allowAnonymous` is demo-only. Product owners (risks, invoices, …) stay `false`.
- Passwords go through `accounts-base` only. Never store them on `nexus_setup` or in applog.
- No `v-html` on untrusted strings. No server fetch of a caller-supplied URL.
- `check` every method/publication argument. Structured selectors only — never string-built queries.

## Config, logging, integrity (A05, A08, A09)

- Do not commit `.env`, PEMs, or generated `settings.json`. Do not put secrets in `Meteor.settings.public`.
- Production must not enable `public.devSeedAdmin`.
- Applog redacts `password`, `bcrypt`, `token`, `services`, `resume`. Add `redactKeys` for anything similar. Do not log secrets.
- Prefer a named helper in this repo over a new dependency for validation or path parsing.

```javascript
// BAD — unreadable and unsafe (client modifier, sync, no role)
Meteor.methods({ 'docs.update'(id, mod) { C.update(id, mod) } })

// GOOD — named gates, async APIs, explicit fields
async 'docs.update'(params) {
  check(params, { id: String, title: String })
  if (!this.userId) throw new Meteor.Error('not-logged-in', 'You must be signed in')
  const allowed = await Roles.userIsInRoleAsync(this.userId, 'docs.update')
  if (!allowed) throw new Meteor.Error('not-authorized', 'Missing role docs.update')
  await C.updateAsync(params.id, { $set: { title: params.title } })
}
```
